cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use FlySweeper, please cite it as below. Any use of the neural wiring it simulates
  must also cite the MaleCNS v1.0 dataset (Berg et al., Cell 2026, CC BY 4.0), listed under
  "references"; see DATA-LICENSE.md.
type: software
title: "FlySweeper: the MaleCNS v1.0 fruit-fly connectome wired to Minesweeper"
abstract: >-
  A whole-connectome leaky integrate-and-fire simulation of the MaleCNS v1.0 Drosophila male
  central nervous system (166,700 neurons, 25,582,938 directed edges) wired to a 9x9 Minesweeper
  board: engineered sensors paint the board onto lamina cells, descending-neuron pools are read as
  buttons, and a helper's board facts are injected as odors so that Kenyon-cell to
  mushroom-body-output-neuron synapses can be trained with a three-factor rule. Includes a
  numba engine, a WebGPU browser port, a seeded validation harness and the trained weight sets.
authors:
  - family-names: Shrivastava
    given-names: Ashutosh
    alias: ASHR12
repository-code: "https://github.com/ASHR12/FlySweeper"
url: "https://github.com/ASHR12/FlySweeper"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-13"
keywords:
  - connectome
  - Drosophila
  - MaleCNS
  - spiking neural network
  - leaky integrate-and-fire
  - mushroom body
  - three-factor learning
  - Minesweeper
  - WebGPU
  - numba
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Sexual dimorphism in the complete connectome of the Drosophila male central nervous system"
    authors:
      - family-names: Berg
        given-names: Stuart
      - name: "et al. (full author list at the DOI)"
    journal: Cell
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.1016/j.cell.2026.08.015
    url: "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2026.08.015"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    notes: >-
      Source of the MaleCNS v1.0 connectome (neurons, connections, cell types, transmitter
      predictions, soma positions, optic-lobe column annotations). Data portal:
      https://male-cns.janelia.org/. FlySweeper redistributes only derived weight files, not
      the source tables.
  - type: article
    title: "A Drosophila computational brain model reveals sensorimotor processing"
    authors:
      - family-names: Shiu
        given-names: Philip K.
      - name: "et al."
    journal: Nature
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.1038/s41586-024-07763-9
    notes: "Whole-brain leaky integrate-and-fire modelling; transmitter sign convention; sensory-input removal."
  - type: software
    title: "Fly64"
    authors:
      - family-names: Paquette
        given-names: Jessica
    url: "https://github.com/ornata/fly"
    notes: "20 ms LIF cartoon, normalized weights, Bernoulli noise, retinal drive formula."
  - type: software
    title: "fly.ai"
    authors:
      - name: alextitonis
    url: "https://github.com/alextitonis/fly.ai"
    notes: "tonic 0.14 / gain 3.0 preset, sensory-input fix, frozen-brain + trained-readout framing."
  - type: software
    title: "DOOMFLY"
    authors:
      - family-names: Wormuth
        given-names: Alex
    url: "https://github.com/nftechie/doomfly"
    notes: "Photoreceptor-to-column mapping via hex-annotated lamina targets, DNpe017 button, PPL1/PAM dopamine poke."
